From ffba440b43043d5974f1fd834971efa99ca555c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:16:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: carried inputs under pool routing (PR 1247
 review notes 2 and 3)

Two non-blocking notes from the independent review of PR 1247 (one worker queue), both
confirmed on main at fbe7656eda before this change:

(3) without_carried_inputs (hermes_cli/kanban_carried_evidence.py) added every heavy_route
value to its destination set as a machine name. A label value such as pool:worker is a
class of machines, so no receipt could ever list it and the carried-input exemption was
off under pool routing (fail closed). A pool label (is_pool_label) in heavy_route or
worker_queue now expands to every registry machine that carries it, held or idle
included, so a machine leaving a hold never runs an input its receipt does not cover.
An unreadable registry, a label with no machines, or a malformed worker_queue still
returns the text unchanged. Machine-name routes are unchanged.

(2) required_labels (hermes_cli/kanban_placement_coordination.py) read the raw body,
while portability's coordination.check reads it after without_carried_inputs. A verified
carried path naming a tool (.../evidence/token-broker-audit/BRIEF.md) passed the
portability check but still added capability:token-broker to the queue's runs_on (and
made legacy_refusal refuse heavy routing). required_labels and legacy_refusal now take
the caller's placement cfg (optional; placement.config() when omitted, as portability
does) and strip carried inputs first. queue_decision and _routeless_heavy pass theirs.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pool_carried_inputs.py. On main 5 tests fail
(the pool-route exemption for heavy_route, worker_queue and with worker_pools; the queue
runs_on; the legacy heavy route), all 12 pass after. Each added condition has a killing
mutant (9/9 killed). The 17 kanban placement test files plus access-contract,
repin-notice and worker-node suites pass.
